Description: numerical library for material laws (development files)
 TFEL is a numerical library developped by CEA and EDF. It provides
 the infrastructure to implement material knowledge (material
 properties, mechanical behaviours, heat transfer laws, etc.) in a way
 which is independent from any solver.
 .
 This package contains the header files required to compile material
 laws generated by MFront and to develop applications using the TFEL
 library, together with the CMake configuration files and the
 tfel-config helper program.
 .
 The development files of the MFront code generator and of the MTest
 solver itself are shipped in the mfront-dev and mtest-dev packages.

Package: mfront
Section: science
Architecture: any
# libtfel-dev is a strict dependency: mfront translates material laws
# into C++ code built on top of the TFEL library and compiling this
# code (which is the normal way to use the generator, with the
# --obuild option or the interactive modes) requires the TFEL header
# files.
Depends:
 libtfel-5.2.0 (= ${binary:Version}),
 libtfel-dev (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
# The material law interfaces require the corresponding solver, which
# is proprietary (Code_Aster, Abaqus, CalculiX, Ansys, Diana FEA,
# Cyrano, Cast3M) and thus not packaged in Debian. The material
# property interfaces require their run time or tool chain: a C++
# compiler to compile the generated code, gfortran for Fortran
# material properties, a JDK for Java material properties, octave and
# gnuplot for material properties written in those languages.
Recommends:
 g++,
 gfortran,
 default-jdk,
 gnuplot,
 octave,
 python3,
Suggests:
 mfront-examples,
 python3-mfront,
Description: code generator for material laws
 MFront is a code generator which translates a set of closely related
 domain specific languages into plain C++ on top of the TFEL library.
 Those languages cover material properties, mechanical behaviours and
 simple point-wise models.
 .
 MFront offers interfaces to finite element solvers such as Cast3M,
 Code_Aster, Abaqus, CalculiX, Ansys, Cyrano, Diana FEA and the MFront
 generic interface. Material properties can additionally be written in
 C, C++, Fortran, Python, Java, Octave or Gnuplot.
 .
 This package contains the MFront code generator and the companion
 tools mfront-query, mfront-doc, tfel-doc, mfm and
 mfm-test-generator. Generating code for a solver requires the solver
 itself; compiling the generated code (for instance with the --obuild
 option) additionally requires a C++ compiler, which MFront detects at
 run time.

Package: mfront-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
# No Multi-Arch: same: the CMake configuration files contain
# architecture dependent paths and are installed in /usr/share.
Depends:
 libtfel-dev (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: development files for the MFront code generator
 MFront is a code generator which translates a set of closely related
 domain specific languages into plain C++ on top of the TFEL library.
 .
 This package contains the header files and the CMake configuration
 files of the MFront libraries: they are required to develop tools
 embedding or extending the MFront code generator (graphical user
 interfaces, alternative front ends, etc.) and to compile the code
 generated for the solvers whose interface ships C++ helper headers
 (Code_Aster, Cast3M, ...). Behaviours written for the MFront generic
 interface only require the TFEL header files (libtfel-dev).

Package: mtest
Section: science
Architecture: any
# mtest is unusable without mfront: it relies on the MFront code
# generator to compile material laws on the fly. The dependency on
# mfront brings the TFEL header files (libtfel-dev), which the
# compiled material laws require.
Depends:
 libtfel-5.2.0 (= ${binary:Version}),
 mfront (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends:
 g++,
 gfortran,
 octave,
 python3,
Suggests:
 python3-mtest,
Description: mechanical testing solver for material laws
 MTest is a unified thermomechanical resolution solver for material
 behaviours. It can run most of the tests conducted in material
 characterization (stress/strain controlled tests, cyclic loading,
 relaxation, creep, etc.) and can be used either as a standalone
 solver or as a post processing tool.
 .
 MTest relies on the MFront code generator to compile material laws on
 the fly. Compiling material laws on the fly additionally requires a
 C++ compiler and the TFEL header files.

Package: mtest-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
# No Multi-Arch: same: the CMake configuration files contain
# architecture dependent paths and are installed in /usr/share.
Depends:
 mfront-dev (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: development files for the MTest solver
 MTest is a unified thermomechanical resolution solver for material
 behaviours.
 .
 This package contains the header files and the CMake configuration
 files of the MTest library and of the MFM test generator library,
 required to develop tools extending MTest (additional tests,
 constraints, post-processings, etc.) or running MTest simulations
 from third party programs.

Package: mfront-examples
Section: doc
Architecture: all
Depends:
 mfront,
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: examples of material laws written with MFront
 MFront is a code generator which translates a set of closely related
 domain specific languages into plain C++ on top of the TFEL library.
 .
 This package contains a gallery of material properties, mechanical
 behaviours and models written with MFront, covering elasticity,
 hyper elasticity, plasticity, visco plasticity, damage, etc.

Package: tfel-check
Section: devel
Architecture: any
Depends:
 libtfel-5.2.0 (= ${binary:Version}),
 mfront (= ${binary:Version}),
 mtest (= ${binary:Version}),
 python3,
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends:
 g++,
Description: validation tool and test suite for TFEL and MFront
 tfel-check runs the TFEL test suite: MFront behaviours, MTest graphs
 and comparison against reference results.
 .
 Install this package to validate a TFEL/MFront installation or to
 get the reference test cases of the TFEL test suite.

Package: python3-tfel
Section: python
Architecture: any
Depends:
 libtfel-5.2.0 (= ${binary:Version}),
 python3,
 python3-numpy,
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: python 3 bindings for the TFEL library
 TFEL is a numerical library to implement material knowledge (material
 properties, mechanical behaviours, heat transfer laws, etc.) in a way
 which is independent from any solver.
 .
 This package contains the python 3 bindings of TFEL: the tfel module
 and its tfel.math, tfel.material and tfel.system submodules expose
 the mathematical types, the behaviours, the material properties and
 the data handling of TFEL to python 3.

Package: python3-mfront
Section: python
Architecture: any
# the mfront.mtest submodule is built on top of the mtest module
Depends:
 libtfel-5.2.0 (= ${binary:Version}),
 python3,
 python3-numpy,
 python3-mtest (= ${binary:Version}),
 python3-tfel (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: python 3 bindings for the MFront code generator
 MFront is a code generator which translates a set of closely related
 domain specific languages into plain C++ on top of the TFEL library.
 .
 This package contains the python 3 bindings of MFront: the mfront
 module allows to write behaviours and material properties in python
 and to use them with MFront or MTest. Its mfront.database submodule
 provides an interface to databases of material properties and the
 mfront.umatxx submodule an interface to UMAT finite element user
 subroutines.

Package: python3-mtest
Section: python
Architecture: any
Depends:
 libtfel-5.2.0 (= ${binary:Version}),
 python3,
 python3-numpy,
 python3-tfel (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: python 3 bindings for the MTest solver
 MTest is a unified thermomechanical resolution solver for material
 behaviours.
 .
 This package contains the python 3 bindings of MTest: the mtest
 module allows to write mechanical tests in python and to run them
 using the MTest solver. The mfm_test_generator module, which converts
 MFM test specifications to MTest tests, is also provided.

Package: tfel-mfront-all
Section: metapackages
Architecture: all
Depends:
 libtfel-5.2.0 (= ${source:Version}),
 libtfel-dev (= ${source:Version}),
 mfront (= ${source:Version}),
 mfront-dev (= ${source:Version}),
 mfront-examples (= ${source:Version}),
 mtest (= ${source:Version}),
 mtest-dev (= ${source:Version}),
 python3-mfront (= ${source:Version}),
 python3-mtest (= ${source:Version}),
 python3-tfel (= ${source:Version}),
 tfel-check (= ${source:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: metapackage for the complete TFEL/MFront tool chain
 This package pulls in all the binary packages built from the TFEL
 sources: the TFEL libraries and their development files, the MFront
 code generator and the MTest solver with their development files,
 their python 3 bindings, the gallery of MFront examples and the TFEL
 test suite.
 .
 Install this package to get a complete TFEL/MFront installation. It
 does not provide any file of its own.
